    "narrative": "For the July 10 slate, the Austin Waves offense is primed for a high-ceiling performance, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88). Facing Avila, **Henderson** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and a 19% SP skill advantage, making him our undisputed top play. **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.89) follows closely, as his favorable platoon split against the left-handed JP Sears provides a significant boost to his base projection. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (75.27) and **Andy Pages** (72.83) capitalize on the soft 5.69 and 4.86 xERA marks of their respective opposing starters; **Pages** is particularly enticing due to the slow delivery of Eduardo Rodriguez, which increases his stolen base equity\u2014a critical component for our team strategy given our focus on speed.\n\nWhile our starting nine remains robust, **Miguel Vargas** (63.96) earns a start in the UTIL slot over the bench options thanks to an elite 0.402 xwOBA, which outweighed the marginal platoon disadvantage against Jacob Lopez. The tightest decision of the day involved **Dominic Smith** (50.40), who was the first player left out of the rotation. Despite his favorable platoon matchup against Kyle Leahy, **Smith** was relegated to the bench because his overall efficiency score failed to clear the threshold established by **Drake Baldwin** and **Josh Jung**, both of whom offer higher positional value today. We are monitoring **Jorge Polanco** closely as a bench asset, though he remains sidelined due to a lower projected efficiency and a 38% rain risk that introduces unnecessary variance. Owners should note that several slots\u2014including **Jackson Merrill**, **Andy Pages**, **Josh Lowe**, **Kyle Tucker**, and **Heliot Ramos**\u2014are currently relying on assumed lineup positions; if these players shift down in the order, their output potential will fluctuate accordingly.",
